# `e2e/php-sapi/seccomp-exec/` is a standalone cargo package (its own
# `[workspace]` table), so `make check` never builds it and the root ignore for
# `/target` does not reach it: a local
# `cargo build --manifest-path e2e/php-sapi/seccomp-exec/Cargo.toml` would drop
# untracked output into the repository.
target/

# The harness lock is **ignored, not committed**: it is a non-published e2e tool
# whose dependency set is exactly `crates/blastit-sys`, so a committed lock would
# churn on every blastit-sys dependency move while pinning nothing that ships.
# The image builds it unlocked on purpose (and the CI job calls clippy without
# `--locked` for the same reason).
Cargo.lock
